doctor, are approaching the patient''s room to
break the news to her when the patient''s son
steps forward and asks you to not tell her
mother about the diagnosis. He argues that
his mother is very fragile at the moment and
that telling her about the diagnosis will make
her worse. You assess the patient''s file. The
consent form does not have any instructions
regarding the patient''s wish as to whether
she wants to be informed of the diagnosis.
