has been under your care for the past eight
years due to chronic obstructive pulmonary
disease (COPD). A few months back she
informed you that she had written a “Do Not
Resuscitate (DNR)” order. Today, he is
brought to you by her family member with a
complaint of severe dyspnea. She looks
drowsy and confused. Her family members
appear quite concerned and ask you to treat
her by any means. Which one of the following
is the most appropriate action?','{"A":"Arrange a family meeting.","B":"Do not give any treatment as she\nhas a DNR order in place.","C":"Admit her and assess for any need\nfor ICU care.","D":"Refer the case to guardianship\ntribunal.","E":"Insert intravenous line and\nnasogastric tube and nothing\nmore."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","supporting_pages":[112,113],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-5e0e7756c842","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"19aeefa0c22c2264a7db","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_page":112,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"19aeefa0c22c2264a7db","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":112,"supporting_pages":[112,113],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Ethics/Population Health","stem":"Sophia is an 82-year-old patient of yours, who\nhas been under your care for the past eight\nyears due to chronic obstructive pulmonary\ndisease (COPD). A few months back she\ninformed you that she had written a “Do Not\nResuscitate (DNR)” order. Today, he is\nbrought to you by her family member with a\ncomplaint of severe dyspnea. She looks\ndrowsy and confused. Her family members\nappear quite concerned and ask you to treat\nher by any means. Which one of the following\nis the most appropriate action?","options":{"A":"Arrange a family meeting.","B":"Do not give any treatment as she\nhas a DNR order in place.","C":"Admit her and assess for any need\nfor ICU care.","D":"Refer the case to guardianship\ntribunal.","E":"Inser